WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.062
Let’s walk through Timeline.

00:00:02.062 --> 00:00:05.037
Use chronology to test sequence, identify gaps, and

00:00:05.037 --> 00:00:07.275
avoid duplicate interpretation.

00:00:07.275 --> 00:00:09.875
The timeline explains how the session developed;

00:00:09.875 --> 00:00:13.725
the owning artifact remains authoritative for current workflow state.

00:00:13.725 --> 00:00:17.150
On this slide, audit the chronological record of artifacts

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:20.663
, RFIs, responses, captures, and updates.

00:00:20.663 --> 00:00:24.288
In practice, use sequence to reconstruct what changed;

00:00:24.288 --> 00:00:27.387
use the artifact surface for current workflow state.

00:00:27.885 --> 00:00:30.735
When you are ready, use Open Timeline to move

00:00:30.735 --> 00:00:32.223
to the live surface.

00:00:32.223 --> 00:00:34.935
The guide will not make the workflow decision for you

00:00:34.935 --> 00:00:35.085
.
